# Architecture Rules

## Core model
- This project follows a compact site architecture.
- Do not expand the page map or navigation without explicit approval.
- Keep architecture focused, trust-oriented, SEO-ready, conversion-oriented.

## Locale strategy
- Final locale model is locked:
  - /uk
  - /ru
  - /en
- Legacy route:
  - /ua/* -> 301 -> /uk/*
- Do not introduce /ua as active canonical locale.

## Slug strategy
- Translated slugs per locale are locked.
- Do not replace them with one shared slug pattern across locales.
- Slug map must be centralized and reusable.

## Core pages
- Home
- Alcohol treatment
- Drug treatment
- Gambling treatment
- Rehabilitation
- Family help
- About center
- Reviews
- FAQ
- Living conditions
- Contacts
- Blog
- Legal pages

## Navigation
Main navigation must remain compact:
- Home
- Services / Treatment container
- Family Help
- About Center
- Reviews
- FAQ
- Contacts

Do not place these as separate first-level main nav items:
- alcohol
- drugs
- gambling
- rehabilitation
- living conditions
- legal pages
- blog in phase 1

## Team page
- No separate team page.
- Team is integrated into About Center.

## Blog
- Blog exists in route structure.
- Blog stays hidden from main navigation in phase 1.

## Data architecture
These systems must be data-driven:
- contacts
- FAQ
- reviews
- gallery
- services content

Do not hardcode reusable content inside shared components.

## Trust structure
- Living conditions is a trust page, not a legal page.
- Reviews, FAQ, About Center, Living Conditions, Contacts are trust/conversion support nodes.

## Internal linking
No page should become a dead end.
Use linking between:
- services
- family help
- reviews
- FAQ
- contacts
- about
- rehabilitation